        "original_id": "1acf059a-6c37-56eb-9f12-877d15521a72",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, James Buchanan, Stephen A. Douglas, Andrew Jackson\n- Places: Michigan, Pennsylvania, Illinois\n- Roles: President, United States Senator, Cabinet member, military officer, politician, statesman\n\nFacts:\n- Lewis Cass was born on October 9, 1782, and died on June 17, 1866.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military officer, politician, and statesman.\n- Lewis Cass represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass served in the Cabinets of Andrew Jackson and James Buchanan.\n- Lewis Cass was the Democratic nominee for President in 1848.\n- The 1852 Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce for President on the 49th ballot.\n- The 1852 Democratic National Convention passed over Lewis Cass of Michigan, James Buchanan of Pennsylvania, and Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois in favor of Franklin Pierce.\n- Franklin Pierce was described as a dark horse candidate at the 1852 Democratic National Convention.",
